# GitHub Copilot Instructions

- Use `uv` for dependency management, virtual environments, and command execution.
- Preserve the layering: `api` (models, schemas, services, dependencies), `core` (config, logging{% if enable_telemetry %}, telemetry{% endif %}{% if enable_azure_auth %}, auth{% endif %}), `database` (session, queues{% if include_example_endpoint %}, repositories{% endif %}), and `routes`.
- Keep all HTTP handlers asynchronous.
- Use SQLAlchemy ORM with `asyncpg`; do not introduce synchronous database access.
- Add Google-style docstrings with explicit types for attributes, arguments, and returns.
- Prefer dependency injection through `src/{{ package_name }}/bootstrap.py` (builder) and `src/{{ package_name }}/container.py` (the `ServiceContainer` shape `api/dependencies.py` type-hints against). `container.py` must not import `api`/`database` modules at runtime — `TYPE_CHECKING` only.
- Route long-running work through queue adapters instead of blocking request handlers. `azure-storage-queue` is an optional extra (`uv sync --extra azure`); import it lazily, not at module scope.
{% if enable_telemetry -%}
- Keep tracing and logging wired through OpenTelemetry-aware helpers in `src/{{ package_name }}/core`.
{% else -%}
- OpenTelemetry is disabled for this project; logging still carries correlation IDs but not trace/span IDs.
{% endif -%}
{% if enable_azure_auth -%}
- Azure Entra ID protects this API: `core/auth.py` builds an `azure_scheme` JWT-validation dependency from the container's settings, exposing `get_current_user` (any valid caller) and `require_role("X")` (app-role gated). Don't parse tokens by hand and don't call `azure_scheme` with real tokens in tests — override `get_current_user` via `app.dependency_overrides`. Only routers that declare `dependencies=[Depends(get_current_user)]` are actually protected — enabling Azure auth doesn't gate a new router by itself.
{% endif -%}
- Type-check with `pyright`, not mypy or `ty`.
- Refresh `.agents/skills` and `.claude/skills` with `uv run library-skills --tool-skill install --claude --yes --all` when dependencies change.
